  "id": "vertical-countermovement-jump",
  "name": "Vertical Countermovement Jump",
  "definition": "A bilateral small hip-and-knee countermovement followed by rapid hip, knee, and ankle extension, flight, and a controlled flexed landing. The exact roster separates a floor-to-20–40 cm box jump with a held receive from a paired side-held dumbbell jump returning to the floor. The box height and dumbbell mass are fixture bounds, not general prescriptions. The step-down reset is supported by NASM technique guidance, not stated by the Boxing Science page. A step-up, depth jump, tuck jump, and unloaded floor CMJ are outside this contract. The box fixture does not pin an arm-swing strategy; only the dumbbell fixture keeps the arms rigid at the sides. Muscle roles are categorical lower-limb anatomy-and-mechanics inferences, not exact-fixture EMG rankings.",
